# Line endings for the build and gate files.
#
# On a machine with core.autocrlf=true a plain checkout rewrites these to CRLF,
# and each one breaks where it is used:
#
#   Makefile        GNU make hands every recipe line to sh with the trailing CR
#                   still attached, and a backslash continuation followed by CR
#                   does not continue — so a multi-line recipe fails in a way
#                   that reads as a shell syntax error, not as a checkout.
#   Dockerfile      every RUN carries a trailing CR into the shell it runs in.
#   .dockerignore   a pattern with a trailing CR matches nothing, silently.
#   *.sh            the loop's mutation suite proves an edit did something by
#                   `sed -i`-ing a copy of claim.sh and `cmp`-ing it against the
#                   original. MSYS2 sed writes a CRLF file back as LF, so the
#                   copy differs on every line whatever the pattern matched, and
#                   an edit that matched nothing is accepted as a real mutation.
#                   Nothing goes red — the misapplication guard just stops
#                   guarding.
#
# None of these is edited to break: the checkout does it, so the diff is empty
# and the file that fails is one nobody touched. `service/.gitattributes` pins
# the module's Go files against the same failure, for the same reason.
#
# These patterns carry no slash, so they match at any depth — the root Makefile
# and service/Dockerfile alike.

Makefile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
*.sh          text eol=lf
